DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ccoouunntteerr is a generic facility to create counters that can be utilized for
     any purpose (such as collecting statistical data).  A ccoouunntteerr is guaran‐
     teed to be lossless when several kernel threads do simultaneous updates.
     However, ccoouunntteerr does not block the calling thread, also no atomic(9) op‐
     erations are used for the update, therefore the counters can be used in
     any non-interrupt context.  Moreover, ccoouunntteerr has special optimisations
     for SMP environments, making ccoouunntteerr update faster than simple arithmetic
     on the global variable.  Thus ccoouunntteerr is considered suitable for account‐
     ing in the performance-critical code paths.

